abstract: >-
  hireburn is a dependency-free Python toolkit for AI-assisted hiring in three parts.
  avatar: a record-once kit for AI-avatar first interviews — recording script and checklist,
  an interview plan of pre-recorded clips with at most one voice-AI follow-up per question,
  a candidate page with mandatory AI disclosure and a consent gate, and a transcript rubric
  whose HIRE / MAYBE / NO labels carry the caveat that a label is not a measurement.
  outreach: personal LinkedIn drafts, a human-pace queue (random pauses, hourly and daily
  caps, working hours, stop on the first warning) worked through by a person who presses
  send, and a reply and follow-up tracker. funnel: losses per stage, show-up and completion
  rates, days to first work, AI label against who is still working on day N, and a candidate
  disclosure checklist measured against NYC Local Law 144, the Illinois AI Video Interview
  Act, Illinois HB 3773 and the EU AI Act. The method comes from a published case report.
